                   ABOUT THE AUTHOR OF THE LIBRARY
          
          Jiri Soukup,  President of Code Farms Inc.,  was one of the
          founding  members   of  CADENCE  Design  Systems  Inc.,   a
          California-based company which is the leader in CAD for VLSI
          circuits.  For 3 years,   he  was  manager of the team that
          developed a program for automatic placement and routing  of
          VLSI  chips.   This  software (about 0.5 million lines of C
          code)  is now being sold  world-wide,   and  is  one of the
          cornerstones of CADENCE's success. Together with Ken Keller,
          Jiri also  designed the original data organization on which
          the CADENCE framework is based today.
          
          In  1980-82,   Jiri  managed   the  LTX2  project  in  Bell
          Laboratories, Murray Hill. LTX2 was the program used for the
          design of the Bellmac32 microprocessor,   and is still used
          today, on a mass scale, in the production of gate arrays and
          standard-cell chips.
          
          Prior to this, Jiri was one of two key designers who created
          the  automatic  system  for the layout of  printed  circuit
          boards in Bell Northern Research, Ottawa. The system is now
          being commercially sold by IBM.
